---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { legal, install } from '../content/site';

const mcpHost = new URL(install.mcpUrl).host;
const mail = `mailto:${legal.email}`;
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Nevo’s Brain collects when you visit nevo.md and when your agent signs in to the MCP server, why, and how to have it deleted."
  other={{ href: '/terms', label: 'terms of service' }}
>
  <p>
    Nevo’s Brain is run by {legal.operator}, the company behind Postiz (“we”, “us”). This policy covers the website
    at nevo.md and the MCP server at {mcpHost} (together, “the service”).
  </p>

  <section class="tldr">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The website has no analytics, no ad trackers and no cookies.</li>
      <li>To use the brain, you sign in with your email. We keep your email and a log of what your agent searches.</li>
      <li>Signing in subscribes you to Nevo’s newsletter. Unsubscribe from any email; you keep your access.</li>
      <li>We don’t sell your data and we don’t show ads.</li>
      <li>Email <a href={mail}>{legal.email}</a> and we will delete everything we hold about you.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>When you visit nevo.md</h3>
  <p>
    The website is a static page. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics or advertising scripts; its fonts and
    videos are served from our own domain. If you pick an agent in “How it works”, your browser remembers that choice
    in its local storage, on your device only. We never receive it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like any web host, our hosting provider records standard request logs (IP address, browser, the page asked for,
    and the time) to run and protect the servers.
  </p>

  <h3>When your agent signs in to the MCP server</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, and when your account was created.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>A 6-digit sign-in code</strong> we email you. It works for 10 minutes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your sign-in session</strong>: the IP address and browser it came from, and the access and refresh
      tokens your agent receives.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The agent app you connected</strong> (for example Claude, ChatGPT or Cursor), as it registers itself:
      its name, ID and callback address.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When your agent uses the brain</h3>
  <p>
    Every call is logged with your account: which tool was used, the search text (up to its first 500 characters),
    which agent app sent it, and when. Your agent writes these searches, and they can describe your product or
    project. Don’t let it send passwords, keys or other people’s personal information.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also use your IP address, in memory and for about a minute, to limit how many requests can be made.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To sign you in and answer your agent’s searches.</li>
    <li>
      To keep the service working for everyone: rate limits (60 calls a minute per person) and blocking accounts that
      abuse it.
    </li>
    <li>
      To improve the brain. Nevo reads what founders ask to learn which questions it answers poorly and what to add
      next.
    </li>
    <li>To send you Nevo’s newsletter (below).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you are in the EU or UK, our legal bases are: providing the service you asked for (sign-in, answers), our
    legitimate interests (security, abuse prevention, improving the brain, and the newsletter, which you can stop at
    any time), and our legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>The newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    Signing in subscribes your email to Nevo’s newsletter, sent through beehiiv. The sign-in page says so before you
    sign in. Every issue has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing doesn’t affect your access to the brain, and signing
    in again never subscribes you again once you have left.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
  <p>We share data only with the providers that run the service for us, and only what each one needs:</p>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">What for</th><th scope="col">What it gets</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Railway</td><td>Hosting and database</td><td>Everything above, stored on its servers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending sign-in codes</td><td>Your email and the code</td></tr>
        <tr><td>beehiiv</td><td>The newsletter</td><td>Your email</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OpenAI</td><td>Matching searches to the brain’s content</td><td>The search text, not who sent it</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Your agent app (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and others) sees your searches and the brain’s answers too. It is run by
    its own company, under its own privacy policy, not ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    We don’t sell or rent personal information, and we don’t share it for advertising. We disclose it to others only
    if the law requires it, to protect the service or its users, or as part of a sale or merger of the business, in
    which case this policy keeps applying to it.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sign-in codes: 10 minutes. Access tokens: one hour; refresh tokens until they expire or are revoked.</li>
    <li>Your account and its search log: until you ask us to delete them.</li>
    <li>The newsletter subscription: until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.</li>
    <li>Hosting request logs: for the short period our hosting provider keeps them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Wherever you live, you can ask us to show you what we hold about you, send you a copy, correct it, or delete it,
    and you can object to how we use it. Email <a href={mail}>{legal.email}</a> from the address you signed in with.
    We answer within 30 days. Deleting your account removes your email, your sessions, your search log and your
    newsletter subscription.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the EU or UK and think we have handled your data wrongly, you can complain to your local data
    protection authority. California residents: we don’t sell or share personal information as the CCPA defines it.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Our providers store and process data in the United States and other countries, which may have different data
    protection laws from yours. For transfers out of the EU and UK we rely on the safeguards our providers offer,
    such as standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Everything travels over HTTPS. There are no passwords to leak: you sign in with a one-time code, tokens are short
    lived and work only for this MCP server, and only Nevo can read the search logs. No system is perfectly secure; if
    we learn of a breach that affects you, we will tell you.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The service is for founders and is not meant for anyone under 16. If you think a child has signed up, email us and
    we will delete the account.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here and change the date at the top. If a change affects how we use
    data we already have, we will email you before it takes effect.
  </p>
</Legal>
